     "\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n<div lang=\"EN-AU\" link=\"blue\" vlink=\"purple\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Hi everyone,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Sorry being basically offline, hence just a quick turnaround.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">To be able to install dartR you need to have PopGenReport. The current way around is to use the archieved.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Version:\r\n<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><a href=\"https://cran.r-project.org/src/contrib/Archive/PopGenReport/PopGenReport_3.0.0.tar.gz\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://cran.r-project.org/src/contrib/Archive/PopGenReport/PopGenReport_3.0.0.tar.gz&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792459419891000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0rh2AOyrsgKstG6nv6jLbW\">https://cran.r-project.org/src/contrib/Archive/PopGenReport/PopGenReport_3.0.0.tar.gz</a><u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">and install it manually (from source) and then install dartR.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Sorry for this I will work on it once back next week.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\">Cheers, Bernd<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><a name=\"m_-600565668824979552__MailEndCompose\" rel=\"nofollow\"><span style=\"font-size:11.0pt;font-family:&quot;Calibri&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;;color:#1f497d\"><u></u> <u></u></span></a></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\">From:</span></b><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size:10.0pt;font-family:&quot;Tahoma&quot;,&quot;sans-serif&quot;\"> Arthur Georges [mailto:<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geo...@aerg.canberra.edu.au</a>]\r\n<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Thursday, 24 January 2019 4:29 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> Bernd.Gruber<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Fwd: dartR installation - problem<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">---------- Forwarded message ---------<br>\r\nFrom: <b>Nina Schwensow</b> &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nina.sc...@uni-ulm.de</a>&gt;<br>\r\nDate: Thu, 24 Jan 2019 at 14:54<br>\r\nSubject: Re: dartR installation - problem<br>\r\nTo: Arthur Georges &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geo...@aerg.canberra.edu.au</a>&gt;<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear Arthur,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Thanks for your email, and yes, the problem seems to be that PopGenReport cannot be installed in R 3.5.2. And without PopGenReport, dartR does not install. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">It would be great if Bernd could have a look after hist return.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Kind regards<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Nina<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Von meinem iPad gesendet<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom:12.0pt\"><br>\r\nAm 24.01.2019 um 00:45 schrieb Arthur Georges &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">geo...@aerg.canberra.edu.au</a>&gt;:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"margin-top:5.0pt;margin-bottom:5.0pt\">\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Dear Nina,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Apologies for this. There seems to be a problem with PopGenReport rather than dartR itself. Bernd is on leave for another week, and will be able to attend to this on his return.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">You could try this:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">install.packages(&quot;devtools&quot;)<br>\r\nlibrary(devtools)<br>\r\ninstall.packages(&quot;BiocManager&quot;)<br>\r\nlibrary(BiocManager)<br>\r\nBiocManager::install(c(&quot;SNPRelate&quot;, &quot;qvalue&quot;))<br>\r\ninstall_github(&quot;green-striped-gecko/PopGenReport&quot;)<br>\r\nlibrary(PopGenReport)<br>\r\ninstall_github(&quot;green-striped-gecko/dartR&quot;)<br>\r\nlibrary(dartR)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">but if that does not work, we will have to wait for Bernd to return.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">Arthur<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<div>\r\n<div>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">On Wed, 23 Jan 2019 at 23:39, Nina Schwensow &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">nina.sc...@uni-ulm.de</a>&gt; wrote:<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n<blockquote style=\"border:none;border-left:solid #cccccc 1.0pt;padding:0cm 0cm 0cm 6.0pt;margin-left:4.8pt;margin-right:0cm\">\r\n<div>\r\n<p>Dear Bernd and Artur,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>I would very much like to try the dartR package but the installations seems to fail because one apparently required package is not available for R 3.5.2 (which I am using). Are you aware of anything I can do to get the dartR installed in spite of it?\r\n<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Kind regards from winterly Germany!<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<p>Nina<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n<pre style=\"background:white;word-break:break-all;outline:currentcolor none medium;white-space:pre-wrap;word-spacing:0px\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">&gt; </span></span><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:blue\">install_github(&quot;green-striped-gecko/dartR&quot;)<u></u><u></u></span></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Downloading GitHub repo green-striped-gecko/dartR@master<u></u><u></u></span></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Skipping 1 packages not available: PopGenReport<u></u><u></u></span></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Skipping 3 packages ahead of CRAN: gdsfmt, qvalue, SNPRelate<u></u><u></u></span></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Installing 53 packages: acepack, base64enc, checkmate, crosstalk, data.table, directlabels, dismo, doParallel, ellipse, evaluate, foreach, Formula, gdistance, gridExtra, haplo.stats, hexbin, highr, Hmisc, htmlTable, htmlwidgets, iterators, knitr, latticeExtra, leaflet, manipulateWidget, markdown, MatrixModels, miniUI, mmod, multcomp, mvtnorm, pca3d, plotly, png, polspline, PopGenReport, quantreg, raster, rgdal, rgl, rms, rrBLUP, sandwich, SNPassoc, SparseM, StAMPP, TH.data, tidyr, viridis, webshot, xfun, yaml, zoo<u></u><u></u></span></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Installing packages into ‘C:/Users/Nina_S/Documents/R/win-library/3.5’<u></u><u></u></span></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">(as ‘lib’ is unspecified)<u></u><u></u></span></span></pre>\r\n<pre style=\"background:white;word-break:break-all\"><span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:#c5060b\">Error: (converted from warning) package ‘PopGenReport’ is not available (for R version 3.5.2)</span></span><span style=\"font-family:&quot;Lucida Console&quot;;color:black\"><u></u><u></u></span></pre>\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n<p><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</blockquote>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n\r\n"
